# What never reaches the build context.
#
# Mostly size and cache hits: a host `node_modules` would be the largest thing
# in the context by far, and copying it in would invalidate the very layer that
# exists so `npm ci` does not run again.

node_modules
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log

# Build output and its caches. Produced inside the image; a stale host copy
# copied in and then half-overwritten is worse than useless.
.next
out
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets --
# This app reads no configuration at all — see the Dockerfile — so an env file
# here would be someone's stray local copy rather than something the build
# needs. An image on a public registry is the last place one should end up,
# where `docker history` would read it straight back out.
.env
.env.*

# Not the app.
.git
.gitignore
.github
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
coverage
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
